# {{name}}

A Sandchart indicator: a WebAssembly module that the app runs in a sandbox. This one
draws a fast and a slow moving average and marks where they cross.

## Build and check

```sh
sandchart-indicator build
sandchart-indicator test target/wasm32-wasip2/release/{{name}}.wasm
```

(For a name with `-`, the file name uses `_`: `my-ind` builds `my_ind.wasm`; the output of
`build` prints the exact path.)

`test` runs the module in the same host the app uses, on 2000 generated bars or on your own
candles (`--csv file.csv`, header `time,open,high,low,close,volume`). Change a parameter with
`--param fast=5`. Use `--json` for machine-readable output. Exit code 0 means it loads and runs;
a line starting with `warning:` is worth reading (for example that the indicator repaints).

## Install in the app

Open Sandchart, then Indicators, then Add from file, and pick the `.wasm` file.

Requires Rust with the `wasm32-wasip2` target (`rustup target add wasm32-wasip2`; the
`rust-toolchain.toml` in this folder asks for it).
